KR2022:183	KR2022	183	<MARKDOWN_START>\nCh 2 Ship Type Notations and Special Feature Notations\n\n## 27-1. Floating Dock\n\n### NOTATIONS (Ship Type Notations)\n\nFloating Dock\n\n### DESCRIPTIONS\n\nFloating Dock : to be assigned to movable docks of which both ends are opened and which are able to control it's draft in large range so that it can be used for the ship's repair, etc. by drawing in a ship into the dock at it's large draft and rising up the ship outside of the water at it's small draft.\n\n### REQUIREMENTS / RULE REFERENCES\n\n| Notations     | Design                          | Survey                          |\n|---------------|----------------------------------|----------------------------------|\n| Floating Dock | Rules for the Classification of Floating Docks | Rules for the Classification of Floating Docks |\n\n### EXAMPLES\n\n※ KRS OS - Floating Dock  \nIWS LG LI\n\nNotation Guide 2022\n<MARKDOWN_END>	Floating Dock
KR2022:184	KR2022	184	<MARKDOWN_START>\nCh 2 Ship Type Notations and Special Feature Notations\n\n## 27-2. Dock Gate\n\n| Ship Type Notations | Special Feature Notations |\n|---------------------|---------------------------|\n| Dock Gate           |                           |\n\n〈 Typical Example 〉\n\n```\n[Symbol] KRS 0 S - [Ship Type Notations]\n                            Dock Gate\n[Special Feature Notations] [Additional Special Feature Notations] [Additional Installations Notations (Hull Items)]\n```\n\n182 Notation Guide 2022\n<MARKDOWN_END>	
